# Every environment variable the API reads (api/main.go). Unset = the default
# shown, so a bare `go run .` needs none of them. Nothing else in the process
# reads the environment, which is what makes local and deployed differ by
# config rather than by code.
#
# `go run .` does not load this file by itself — export the variables, or pass
# them to the process (docker compose reads its own env; see the root README).

# HTTP port the API listens on.
PORT=8080

# Seed for the market generator: same seed, same trades, same candles. A value
# that is not an integer is a startup error, never a silent fallback.
SEED=42

# Symbol reported by GET /api/config and rendered on screen. The feed itself is
# one simulated market.
SYMBOL=BTC-USD

# Per-connection delivery bands (docs/SPEC.md Bullet 3). RTT/2 at or below
# TIER_FULL_MAX_MS with jitter at or below TIER_MAX_JITTER_MS is full tier; at
# or below TIER_DEGRADED_MAX_MS is degraded; past that is minimal.
# 3 consecutive worse probes step down, 5 better ones step up (per connection),
# and a client that stops reporting for 3 windows degrades, 6 minimizes.
TIER_FULL_MAX_MS=150
TIER_DEGRADED_MAX_MS=300
TIER_MAX_JITTER_MS=50
TIER_DOWN_VOTES=3
TIER_UP_VOTES=5
TIER_MISS_DEGRADED=3
TIER_MISS_MINIMAL=6
